  "notes": "{表|あらわ}れる is an intransitive ichidan verb. The key distinction from {現|あらわ}れる is that {表|あらわ}れる is used when something abstract or internal becomes externally visible, while {現|あらわ}れる describes physical appearance or emergence.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{表|あらわ}れている indicates that something is currently visible or showing.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～が{表|あらわ}れる (something shows/manifests)\n- ～に{表|あらわ}れる (shows in/on something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {効果|こうか}が{表|あらわ}れる (effects show)\n- {結果|けっか}に{表|あらわ}れる (show in the results)\n- {態度|たいど}に{表|あらわ}れる (show in one's attitude)\n- {症状|しょうじょう}が{表|あらわ}れる (symptoms manifest)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {現|あらわ}れる: to appear, to emerge (physical appearance of a person or thing)\n- {出|で}る: to come out (more general, everyday usage)",
